menu "MyEMS Modbus RTU"

config MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST
    bool "Run Modbus RTU self-test instead of normal polling"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the firmware runs a sequential test suite against the
        configured Modbus RTU slave simulator. When disabled, normal meter
        polling is started. Enable this only when connected to the test simulator.

config MYEMS_CONFIG_TARGET_SIM
    bool "DP-WP4 simulation build (accept SIMULATION_ONLY / TEST_ONLY configuration)"
    depends on !MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST
    default n
    help
        Set only in sdkconfig.wp4_sim. The firmware then accepts the generated
        configuration only if it was generated with --target sim, and refuses
        to poll otherwise; a production build (this option off) accepts only
        PRODUCTION configurations generated with --target prod
        (DP-WP4 Design rule V-13). Simulation configurations use synthetic
        register addresses: connect only the MyEMS simulator.

config MYEMS_WP4_ESC_TEST
    bool "DP-WP4 D8 escalation test build (forces RS-485 recovery to fail)"
    depends on MYEMS_CONFIG_TARGET_SIM
    select MYEMS_WP24_FAULT_INJECTION
    default n
    help
        Set only in sdkconfig.wp4_esc (Test Spec ESC-001: "force RS-485
        recovery FAILED (test hook)"). At start-up the firmware arms the
        transport hook rs485_test_force_recovery_activity(), so the next
        RS-485 recovery never sees bus silence and fails; the first failed
        transaction then takes the bus to BUS_FAULT. Everything after the
        transport (master fail-closed path, bus health, scheduler hold,
        device state) is the normal code. Simulation builds only.

config MYEMS_WP24_FAULT_INJECTION
    bool "Enable WP2.4 extended recovery test hooks"
    depends on MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST || MYEMS_WP4_ESC_TEST
    default n
    help
        Enables test-only RS485 event injection and recovery-activity forcing.
        Keep disabled in every production configuration.

config MYEMS_WP24_EXTENDED_TEST
    int "WP2.4 test selection (0=off, 1=retry, 2=RX loss, 3=recovery timeout, 4=all A-I, 5=retry exhaustion, 6=retry exhaustion/request isolation, 7=WP24-L, 8=WP24-M1, 9=WP24-M2)"
    depends on MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST && MYEMS_WP24_FAULT_INJECTION
    range 0 9
    default 0
    help
        Select one extended test, WP24-J retry exhaustion, WP24-K request isolation, WP24-L stale-response guard, WP24-M1 pre-boundary, WP24-M2 post-boundary, or the complete A-I campaign for this dedicated self-test firmware build.
        These tests require the USB-RS485 simulator, never a live meter.


config MYEMS_WP24_CASE_SELECTION
    int "WP24 isolated case selection (0=full campaign, 1=A, 2=B, 3=C, 4=D, 5=E, 6=F)"
    depends on MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST && MYEMS_WP24_FAULT_INJECTION
    range 0 6
    default 0
    help
        Select one WP24-A through WP24-F fault-injection case for isolated validation.
        0 runs the existing full A-I campaign. Values 1..6 run only the selected
        A-F case and its address-200 isolation/control request. Use only with the
        USB-RS485 simulator, never a live meter.

config MYEMS_WP25_D_TEST
    bool "Run WP2.5-D pending-request cancellation test"
    depends on MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST
    default n
    help
        Runs a cancellation test with one active request and two queued requests.
        Do not connect a live meter or simulator; requests are intentionally
        cancelled before a response is expected.

endmenu


config MYEMS_WP25_B2_TEST
    bool "Run WP2.5-B2 active shutdown and completion-drain test"
    depends on MYEMS_MODBUS_SELF_TEST
    default n
    help
        Tests stop with one active and two queued requests, terminal cancellation
        completions, DRAINING state, post-stop completion draining, idempotent
        repeated stop, and rejection of new submissions. Disconnect the RS485
        simulator and never connect a live meter during this test.
